From: theycallmeboxy <82409831+theycallmeboxy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 21:10:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] panvk/csf: elide redundant barrier syncs and idle compute
 subqueue work

Graphics barriers (render pass dependencies, layout transitions, most
"render target becomes a texture" barriers) usually have ALL_COMMANDS or
all shader stages in a scope, so every barrier made all three subqueues
self-wait, flush and signal, and wait on each other, even when the compute
subqueue never runs anything. Within a primary command buffer:

- A wait on a sync point a subqueue already waited for unconditionally is
  skipped (sync points only grow, each subqueue runs in order).
- A barrier cache flush is skipped when the subqueue emitted nothing but
  barrier syncs since a flush that covers it (flushes already come before
  a barrier's waits).
- A compute subqueue that did nothing since its last barrier signal but wait
  is idle: it skips its self-wait and signal (that signal still covers its
  work), and subqueues that would wait on it wait on what it waited for
  instead, so dependency chains through it hold.
- An idle compute subqueue defers its waits and cache flushes from
  vkCmdPipelineBarrier2 until it is next used (panvk_get_cs_builder()): a
  blocked wait is re-checked on every signal of the subqueue it waits on.
  At the end of the command buffer the waits are dropped (the flush is
  kept); every primary starts with the compute subqueue owing waits on all
  earlier vertex/tiler and fragment work.

PANVK_NO_SYNC_ELISION=1 turns this off.

